// What a fight pays and what things cost, tuned while the game runs.
//
// The game reads this file again whenever it is saved (BIMS_REWARDS names
// another). The next enemy down and the next price asked take the new
// numbers. A field left out is the built-in value, and a file that does not
// parse keeps the last good numbers (the reason is printed on the terminal).
//
//   xp_per_down             experience for an enemy down or destroyed, once,
//                           to every classed crew member within fifty tiles
//   bounty                  money for an enemy down or destroyed, once, by
//                           the tier of its gear (a machine: its own tier):
//                           tier one, two, three
//   defense_bounty_percent  how much of that a defence pays (100 = the same
//                           as an attack, 0 = nothing)
//   bounty_waits_for_clear  true: the money waits until the site is cleared
//                           and is lost if the crew leave first;
//                           false: paid the moment the enemy goes down
//   buyback                 what bringing a dead player's Bim back costs
//   relic_price             a trader's relic, by its tier: one, two, three
//   combine_fee             combining two things into the next tier
//   shelf_price_percent     a trader's shelf prices, in per cent
//
// The values below are the built-in ones.
(
    xp_per_down: 20,
    bounty: (500, 1500, 4500),
    defense_bounty_percent: 100,
    bounty_waits_for_clear: true,
    buyback: 5000,
    relic_price: (1500, 3000, 5000),
    combine_fee: 0,
    shelf_price_percent: 100,
)
